  "production_date": "about 1480-5",
  "brief_description": "The Virgin Mary kneels in adoration before Christ, her son, who lies on his back in the hay in a manger. Behind her are two men in ragged clothes. This is the Adoration of the Shepherds, described in Gospel of Luke (2: 8--18). Mary's husband Joseph -- looking slightly despondent -- sits huddled in a yellow cloak, his back against the wall. Beside him, a small waterskin and a round object, perhaps a flask, hang from a peg.\n\nThis small panel is one of a series that shows events from the life of Christ, painted by Bernardino Butinone probably in the early 1480s. Around 13 survive in various collections; others are lost. They perhaps came from a large multi-panelled altarpiece that possibly involved sculpture, such as were fashionable in Lombardy.",
